  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer planar stack on Al substrate with air incidence. Stack sequence: Cr | HfO2 | SiO2 | Cr | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2. Initialize thicknesses from round 4 best candidate [10, 126, 97, 21, 52, 25, 132, 110, 65, 75, 210, 28, 81, 155, 46, 60, 141, 44, 82, 91] nm. Apply optimization bounds of +/-50 nm around initialization for layers 0-3 (Cr interfaces) and +/-30 nm for layers 4-8 (high-gradient dielectric pairs), +/-100 nm for layers 9-19. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with learning rate reduced by 50% from standard. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized, wavelength bands 400-700 nm (minimize reflectance) and 700-2000 nm (maximize reflectance). Total layer count fixed at 20. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
